{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The repaired consumer must remain running across producer disconnects and accept jobs from successive producers without a consumer restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same consumer PID remained alive after two separate producers connected and disconnected, both before and after the node restart; each producer's job was recorded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9dea37af1dae42ed","cmd-ff44709ea851418a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Record complete newline-delimited job IDs, ignore empty and unterminated lines, and retain previous records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests recorded each submitted complete non-empty line exactly once, rejected empty and incomplete input, and preserved the original previous-job record as the first entry through all later tests and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4287affd7bb4ed3","cmd-9dea37af1dae42ed","cmd-ff44709ea851418a","cmd-6751d46fed5e4cf7"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Avoid a busy loop while no producer is connected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During disconnected intervals the consumer was sleeping in wait_for_partner and accumulated zero CPU ticks over measured idle periods, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9dea37af1dae42ed","cmd-ff44709ea851418a"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Provide a clean SIGTERM shutdown.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SIGTERM stopped the consumer with status 0, left no error-log output, and left no consumer process, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9dea37af1dae42ed","cmd-ff44709ea851418a","cmd-e1eaac5fc6924f00","cmd-6751d46fed5e4cf7"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The Python-only repair compiled and executed successfully with the installed Python 3.12.9.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e1a3cf6ecd374ca6","cmd-f32148f1aef94f6f","cmd-6751d46fed5e4cf7","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The pre-change submission reproduced the defect; script replacement and metadata restoration implemented the repair; subsequent submissions collected bounded functional and restart evidence; temporary backups and logs were removed. Verification records appropriately remained because the task requires retained records. The mandatory reboot was acknowledged, produced a different boot identity, and was followed by recovered SSH, data, FIFO behavior, and clean system state. Final observations show no failed services, new exposure, package damage, or abandoned temporary artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e482c0a9555c4e22","cmd-f32148f1aef94f6f","cmd-9dea37af1dae42ed","cmd-f48ecdecbbc149b8","cmd-b8f64b7d02e14051","cmd-f2a837c1983a49cc","cmd-ff44709ea851418a","cmd-6751d46fed5e4cf7","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is also complete and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, changed boot ID, and recovered access, data, and consumer behavior were observed.","limitations":[]}
